## Research Highlights
1. The 3D metal oxide $@$ MOFs nanoarray ( $\mathrm{Cu}_{2}\mathrm{O}@$ Cu-MOF/copper mesh) was prepared by the in-situ generation method, which solved the problems of low conductivity and disordered orientation of MOFs.
2. The detection sensitivity could be further improved based on Exo III-assisted target cycle amplification strategy combined with RCA reaction to obtain DNAzymes as signal amplifier.
3. The strategy not only provides a new way for sensitive target detection, but also expands the application of semiconductor $@$ MOFs in the field of PEC sensing.
